  "unmapped_findings": [
    "For the overaged sample (overaging treatment at 625 °C for 192 h), the κ-carbide particles are observed and sheared by the planar dislocation band; the large size and high-volume fraction of the κ-carbide particles introduce limited chances of particles being sheared by planar dislocations, resulting in lower work hardening capacity compared with that of the short-time aging treated sample (aging time less than 10 h). The review concludes that the SRO strengthening mechanism is strongly influenced by the κ phase precipitation, thus the longtime aging treatment shall be avoided. (b0071)"
  ]
